---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { edgeFunctions } from '../data/release';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Architecture"
  description="How PAUSE AI keeps notification decisions local while using Supabase and Qwen as consented supporting systems."
>
  <section class="page-hero shell" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">System design · six stages</p>
    <h1 id="architecture-title">AI advises. Your boundary decides.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      PAUSE is an Android-first boundary broker—not a messenger. It observes selected notifications,
      applies deterministic policy on the device, and uses cloud guidance only within explicit account
      and consent boundaries.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="shell architecture-section" aria-labelledby="flow-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Decision path</p>
        <h2 id="flow-title">One interruption. Clear trust boundaries.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Follow the numbered path. The labels—not color—identify where data is handled and who keeps authority.</p>
    </div>

    <figure class="architecture-flow">
      <div class="flow-zones" aria-label="Processing zones">
        <span class="zone-local">On your device · stages 1–3</span>
        <span class="zone-cloud">Consented cloud · stages 4–5</span>
        <span class="zone-advisory">Advice only · stage 6</span>
      </div>
      <ol>
        <li class="flow-card local">
          <span class="step">01</span>
          <span class="flow-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="stage-place">Device</p>
          <h3>Android listener</h3>
          <p>Receives notifications only from apps the person explicitly allows PAUSE to monitor.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-card local">
          <span class="step">02</span>
          <span class="flow-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="stage-place">Local</p>
          <h3>Policy engine</h3>
          <p>Checks the active boundary, exceptions, urgency rules, and pause state before any AI request.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-card local">
          <span class="step">03</span>
          <span class="flow-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="stage-place">Local</p>
          <h3>SQLite + SecureStore</h3>
          <p>Keeps the broker responsive and protects private device state, even when the network is absent.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-card cloud">
          <span class="step">04</span>
          <span class="flow-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="stage-place">Consented cloud</p>
          <h3>Supabase + RLS</h3>
          <p>Authenticates the owner and limits synchronized rows to that owner at the database boundary.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-card cloud">
          <span class="step">05</span>
          <span class="flow-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="stage-place">Consented cloud</p>
          <h3>Edge Functions</h3>
          <p>Validate requests, enforce privacy settings, and keep AI provider credentials off the device.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="flow-card advisory">
          <span class="step">06</span>
          <span class="flow-node" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="stage-place">Advisory</p>
          <h3>Qwen guidance</h3>
          <p>Returns classification or digest guidance. Deterministic local policy still chooses the action.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <figcaption>
        Stages 1–3 remain useful without Cloud AI. Account sync and AI processing are bounded separately;
        an unavailable or uncertain provider never becomes permission to bypass local rules.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="shell principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="principles-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Failure posture</p>
      <h2 id="principles-title">Calm when every dependency works. Safe when one does not.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="trust-mark" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h3>Local authority</h3>
        <p>Explicit rules and exceptions override uncertain or unavailable AI output.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="trust-mark" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h3>Owner isolation</h3>
        <p>Row Level Security limits cloud reads and writes to the authenticated owner.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="trust-mark" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h3>Honest fallback</h3>
        <p>Network ambiguity becomes a safe deterministic result—not a fabricated AI success.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell functions" aria-labelledby="functions-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Release evidence</p>
      <h2 id="functions-title">Nine deployed Edge Functions</h2>
      <p class="functions-intro">Small, named server boundaries keep privileged work inspectable.</p>
    </div>
    <ul>
      {edgeFunctions.map((name) => <li><code>{name}</code></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="fine-print">Names are public release evidence. Provider responses, credentials, and application source remain private.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    max-width: 1000px;
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem) clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .architecture-section,
  .principles,
  .functions {
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: end;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .section-heading > p,
  .functions-intro {
    max-width: 52ch;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .architecture-flow {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .flow-zones,
  .architecture-flow ol {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .flow-zones {
    gap: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .flow-zones span {
    padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font: 0.65rem/1.35 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.055em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .zone-local {
    grid-column: span 3;
    color: var(--color-calm);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-calm) 9%, transparent);
  }

  .zone-cloud {
    grid-column: span 2;
    color: var(--color-focus);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-focus) 9%, transparent);
  }

  .zone-advisory {
    color: var(--color-alert);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-alert) 9%, transparent);
  }

  .architecture-flow ol {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    list-style: none;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .architecture-flow ol::before {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    top: 69px;
    right: 8.3%;
    left: 8.3%;
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-calm) 0 50%, var(--color-focus) 50% 83.3%, var(--color-alert) 83.3%);
    content: '';
  }

  .flow-card {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 320px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .flow-card:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .flow-card.cloud {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-focus) 6%, var(--color-surface));
  }

  .flow-card.advisory {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-alert) 6%, var(--color-surface));
  }

  .step {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font: 0.66rem/1 var(--font-mono);
  }

  .flow-node {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    display: block;
    width: 13px;
    height: 13px;
    margin: 1.45rem auto 1.6rem;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-calm);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--color-calm);
  }

  .cloud .flow-node {
    background: var(--color-focus);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--color-focus);
  }

  .advisory .flow-node {
    background: var(--color-alert);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--color-alert);
  }

  .stage-place {
    min-height: 2.3em;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-privacy);
    font: 0.63rem/1.35 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.055em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .flow-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .flow-card > p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  figcaption {
    max-width: 88ch;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .principles-heading {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .trust-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .trust-grid article {
    min-height: 230px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface) 82%, transparent);
  }

  .trust-mark {
    color: var(--color-privacy);
    font: 0.72rem/1 var(--font-mono);
  }

  .trust-grid h3 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .trust-grid p {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .functions {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
    gap: 1.5rem 3rem;
    padding-bottom: clamp(6rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }

  .functions ul {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .functions li {
    padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .functions code {
    color: var(--color-calm);
  }

  .fine-print {
    grid-column: 2;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .flow-zones {
      display: none;
    }

    .architecture-flow ol {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      overflow: visible;
    }

    .architecture-flow ol::before {
      top: 42px;
      right: auto;
      bottom: 42px;
      left: 38px;
      width: 1px;
      height: auto;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-calm) 0 50%, var(--color-focus) 50% 83.3%, var(--color-alert) 83.3%);
    }

    .flow-card {
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    }

    .flow-card:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .step {
      position: absolute;
      top: 1.65rem;
      left: 1.15rem;
      z-index: 3;
      width: 38px;
      color: var(--color-ink);
      text-align: center;
    }

    .flow-node {
      position: absolute;
      top: 1.45rem;
      left: 31px;
      margin: 0;
      opacity: 0.35;
    }

    .stage-place {
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .section-heading,
    .functions {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .trust-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .trust-grid article {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .trust-grid h3 {
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .fine-print {
      grid-column: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
